WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.220
- So I was watching this Woody Allen film

00:00:02.220 --> 00:00:05.400
called "Hannah and Her
Sisters," and in the movie,

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:08.580
there's this scene where Michael
Kane's character, Elliot,

00:00:08.580 --> 00:00:11.490
is sitting at the dinner
table with his wife, Hannah.

00:00:11.490 --> 00:00:14.490
Now, Elliot is completely
emotionally detached,

00:00:14.490 --> 00:00:17.730
he is disturbed, and that's
because he's been having

00:00:17.730 --> 00:00:19.770
an affair with his wife's sister.

00:00:19.770 --> 00:00:21.090
Shocking stuff, I know.

00:00:21.090 --> 00:00:23.070
But this scene really got me thinking

00:00:23.070 --> 00:00:27.030
about the way in which a lot
of us live our entire lives,

00:00:27.030 --> 00:00:30.180
hopefully not by having affairs
with our wife's sisters,

00:00:30.180 --> 00:00:32.822
but what I mean is that
we do certain things

00:00:32.822 --> 00:00:36.750
or leave certain things undone in the past

00:00:36.750 --> 00:00:39.810
that continue to eat
away at us subconsciously

00:00:39.810 --> 00:00:40.680
in the present.

00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:43.530
And a lot of the time, we
do this so compulsively

00:00:43.530 --> 00:00:45.960
that we don't even know
that we're doing it.

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:49.440
We just see it as normal,
we don't know anything else,

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:52.830
yet we're living a lower
quality of life because of it.

00:00:52.830 --> 00:00:54.570
Every single thing that we do,

00:00:54.570 --> 00:00:56.850
every single conversation that we have

00:00:56.850 --> 00:00:59.700
is infected by the things that we've left

00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:01.890
usually undone in the past.

00:01:01.890 --> 00:01:05.340
And I think this is the
most insidiously toxic thing

00:01:05.340 --> 00:01:07.890
about escapism and procrastination,

00:01:07.890 --> 00:01:09.210
and that is because of something

00:01:09.210 --> 00:01:11.670
I like to call mental air time.

00:01:11.670 --> 00:01:15.630
When we haven't yet done what
we know we're supposed to do

00:01:15.630 --> 00:01:18.870
and we have a tendency
to put these things off

00:01:18.870 --> 00:01:23.430
every single day, then we
exist in a mental framework

00:01:23.430 --> 00:01:26.760
where we are a person who
hasn't yet done the thing

00:01:26.760 --> 00:01:27.930
that we're supposed to do.

00:01:27.930 --> 00:01:30.090
And over a long period of time,

00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:34.380
this really changes how we
feel about our entire lives,

00:01:34.380 --> 00:01:36.000
because no matter what we're doing,

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:38.190
no matter what kind of
conversation we're having,

00:01:38.190 --> 00:01:39.900
no matter how special the person

00:01:39.900 --> 00:01:42.030
we're having that conversation with is,

00:01:42.030 --> 00:01:44.730
we are subconsciously tainted by the fact

00:01:44.730 --> 00:01:47.160
that we are not where
we're supposed to be,

00:01:47.160 --> 00:01:49.500
we are not being who we're supposed to be.

00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:51.600
And we live our entire lives like this

00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:55.410
emotionally disturbed with
this feeling of anxiety

00:01:55.410 --> 00:01:59.340
that's just always there
because of our chronic escapism.

00:01:59.340 --> 00:02:02.880
People don't talk about
procrastination this way, it's nuts,

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:06.120
because when we procrastinate,
it's not just the thing

00:02:06.120 --> 00:02:08.430
that we're supposed to do that suffers,

00:02:08.430 --> 00:02:10.458
everything else suffers as well

00:02:10.458 --> 00:02:12.540
because we're not present with it,

00:02:12.540 --> 00:02:15.540
we don't have the mental
capacity to enjoy it.

00:02:15.540 --> 00:02:18.780
Anything good in our lives
is infected with this feeling

00:02:18.780 --> 00:02:22.020
like it's not good enough,
we're not supposed to be here

00:02:22.020 --> 00:02:23.460
because there's that other thing

00:02:23.460 --> 00:02:24.870
that we're supposed to be doing.

00:02:24.870 --> 00:02:25.980
And the weird thing is,

00:02:25.980 --> 00:02:28.620
it's not like we're never
going to do that thing,

00:02:28.620 --> 00:02:30.330
we usually end up doing it.

00:02:30.330 --> 00:02:32.820
Usually the deadline comes closer,

00:02:32.820 --> 00:02:35.970
the repercussions for not
doing it grows scarier

00:02:35.970 --> 00:02:37.380
and more acute,

00:02:37.380 --> 00:02:40.860
so we eventually guilt ourselves
into eventually doing it

00:02:40.860 --> 00:02:43.680
so that we can repeat that
cycle every single day

00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:44.940
for the rest of our lives.

00:02:44.940 --> 00:02:48.510
But what's crazy is since
we end up doing it anyways,

00:02:48.510 --> 00:02:51.561
there's great utility to
just changing the order

00:02:51.561 --> 00:02:53.370
in which we do things.

00:02:53.370 --> 00:02:56.610
We can escape and do all of
the other bullshit later,

00:02:56.610 --> 00:02:58.530
but if we could find a way

00:02:58.530 --> 00:03:01.080
to do the the most important
thing that we need to do

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:02.280
earlier in the day,

00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:05.700
then we could change the
entire narrative of our lives.

00:03:05.700 --> 00:03:08.790
We could change the way
we feel about ourselves,

00:03:08.790 --> 00:03:11.250
about our capability to solve problems.

00:03:11.250 --> 00:03:13.290
And the theme of our lives that's echoing

00:03:13.290 --> 00:03:15.480
through our subconscious becomes,

00:03:15.480 --> 00:03:19.620
oh yes, I can play video
games, I can watch this movie,

00:03:19.620 --> 00:03:21.450
I can enjoy this conversation,

00:03:21.450 --> 00:03:24.420
because I've already done the
thing that I'm supposed to do.

00:03:24.420 --> 00:03:27.270
So how do we do it? That's
the golden question.

00:03:27.270 --> 00:03:29.880
Well, knowing what it's
doing to us is great

00:03:29.880 --> 00:03:32.730
and I think this will help
you get some motivation

00:03:32.730 --> 00:03:36.210
to just do the damn thing,
but when push comes to shove,

00:03:36.210 --> 00:03:38.220
this is an irrational problem.

00:03:38.220 --> 00:03:40.650
I can give you all the
rationality in the world

00:03:40.650 --> 00:03:42.390
but when you're faced with the crossroads

00:03:42.390 --> 00:03:45.570
of watching this funny
little YouTube video

00:03:45.570 --> 00:03:47.760
versus writing a research paper,

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:50.010
something other than logic takes over.

00:03:50.010 --> 00:03:52.530
Your monkey brain kind of
bullies your rational brain

00:03:52.530 --> 00:03:54.840
into coming up with a rationalization

00:03:54.840 --> 00:03:57.750
to justify some suboptimal behavior.

00:03:57.750 --> 00:04:00.180
So the answer can't be logical.

00:04:00.180 --> 00:04:03.030
It has to be an emotional tactic

00:04:03.030 --> 00:04:06.750
and I think that tactic is submission.

00:04:06.750 --> 00:04:07.593
- Submission.

00:04:11.101 --> 00:04:12.570
You know, that's a bit of a problem.

00:04:12.570 --> 00:04:14.730
- Nobody talks about this word submission

00:04:14.730 --> 00:04:16.800
in a productivity context.

00:04:16.800 --> 00:04:19.230
They talk about it in other contexts

00:04:19.230 --> 00:04:21.600
but we're not gonna get
into those other contexts.

00:04:21.600 --> 00:04:23.010
That's not what this channel's about.

00:04:23.010 --> 00:04:27.240
What I mean by submission,
it is a feeling of melting

00:04:27.240 --> 00:04:29.310
into what you're supposed to be doing.

00:04:29.310 --> 00:04:31.560
It's not increasing the
tension in your body

00:04:31.560 --> 00:04:34.560
to try to fight and
bully your monkey brain

00:04:34.560 --> 00:04:37.080
into doing what your more logical side

00:04:37.080 --> 00:04:38.370
of your brain wants it to do.

00:04:38.370 --> 00:04:40.620
No, it's acknowledging

00:04:40.620 --> 00:04:44.460
that doing what you're
supposed to do feels difficult,

00:04:44.460 --> 00:04:47.040
it's feeling that tension
that's stopping you

00:04:47.040 --> 00:04:49.440
from doing that thing,
and letting go of it,

00:04:49.440 --> 00:04:50.880
and doing the thing anyways.

00:04:50.880 --> 00:04:54.120
We need to get good at
shutting the brain off,

00:04:54.120 --> 00:04:58.620
stopping the chatter of
rationalization and escapism,

00:04:58.620 --> 00:05:01.260
reduce the tension in our body,

00:05:01.260 --> 00:05:05.340
take a deep breath, and just do the thing.

00:05:05.340 --> 00:05:09.060
We can think about all the
rationalizations afterwards.

00:05:09.060 --> 00:05:11.880
But submitting to what you already know

00:05:11.880 --> 00:05:13.230
you're supposed to be doing

00:05:13.230 --> 00:05:15.780
is less of a psychological feeling,

00:05:15.780 --> 00:05:17.910
it's more of a physiological feeling.

00:05:17.910 --> 00:05:20.430
And again, this might sound very woo-woo,

00:05:20.430 --> 00:05:22.800
but if you've ever tried
to take cold showers

00:05:22.800 --> 00:05:25.230
or go cliff jumping with your friends,

00:05:25.230 --> 00:05:26.370
it's the same feeling.

00:05:26.370 --> 00:05:29.580
You almost submit to the discomfort.

00:05:29.580 --> 00:05:31.500
If you're standing there
at the edge of the cliff

00:05:31.500 --> 00:05:32.730
and you don't want to jump,

00:05:32.730 --> 00:05:35.010
even though you know it's perfectly safe,

00:05:35.010 --> 00:05:38.190
it's a very steep drop
off, very deep water,

00:05:38.190 --> 00:05:40.170
nothing could happen to you.

00:05:40.170 --> 00:05:44.040
You almost need to just
submit to the gravity.

00:05:44.040 --> 00:05:45.660
Same thing with cold showers.

00:05:45.660 --> 00:05:47.670
If you already know you're going to enter

00:05:47.670 --> 00:05:51.030
into the cold shower and
feel very uncomfortable,

00:05:51.030 --> 00:05:53.460
the only way that you're
gonna get in there

00:05:53.460 --> 00:05:56.070
is if you just walk in.

00:05:56.070 --> 00:05:59.040
You stop the chatter, you stop thinking.

00:05:59.040 --> 00:06:00.870
The mind is corrosive.

00:06:00.870 --> 00:06:03.600
It'll try to figure out all
these different little ways

00:06:03.600 --> 00:06:05.940
to weasel out of it and
you don't end up doing it.

00:06:05.940 --> 00:06:09.450
It's like if you already know
this is what you must do,

00:06:09.450 --> 00:06:12.840
relax your body and submit to it.

00:06:12.840 --> 00:06:14.520
And while you're in the cold shower,

00:06:14.520 --> 00:06:18.840
it feels so much colder if
you maintain this resistance,

00:06:18.840 --> 00:06:20.670
if you try to fight the cold,

00:06:20.670 --> 00:06:22.140
if you tense up your body

00:06:22.140 --> 00:06:26.550
and you try to convince
yourself to power through it.

00:06:26.550 --> 00:06:30.540
It's so much better if you
just concentrate on the cold,

00:06:30.540 --> 00:06:33.900
you fully submit to it,
you fully focus on it,

00:06:33.900 --> 00:06:36.030
and you accept the fact that it's cold,

00:06:36.030 --> 00:06:38.130
and then it ceases to be so cold.

00:06:38.130 --> 00:06:42.090
You're allowing yourself to
relax into this discomfort,

00:06:42.090 --> 00:06:44.520
and it actually feels quite
euphoric when you do that.

00:06:44.520 --> 00:06:47.790
I think this is the key
to stop procrastinating.

00:06:47.790 --> 00:06:48.870
I think this is the key

00:06:48.870 --> 00:06:51.300
to make better decisions in the moment.

00:06:51.300 --> 00:06:53.760
You've already heard the logical reasons

00:06:53.760 --> 00:06:55.410
as to why you should do the thing

00:06:55.410 --> 00:06:56.820
that you're supposed to do.

00:06:56.820 --> 00:07:00.240
You know that your life
will be dramatically better

00:07:00.240 --> 00:07:03.420
if the majority of the time
you spend here on this Earth,

00:07:03.420 --> 00:07:06.660
you exist in a head space
where you have already done

00:07:06.660 --> 00:07:08.820
the most important thing
that you need to do.

00:07:08.820 --> 00:07:11.580
You already know that
this is so good for you.

00:07:11.580 --> 00:07:14.430
The only step now is
when you're confronted

00:07:14.430 --> 00:07:18.360
with the crossroads is to
just turn the brain off,

00:07:18.360 --> 00:07:20.880
to submit to what you're supposed to do.

00:07:20.880 --> 00:07:23.790
It's like submitting to the
highest version of yourself

00:07:23.790 --> 00:07:25.650
and you start to develop trust

00:07:25.650 --> 00:07:27.750
that that highest version of yourself

00:07:27.750 --> 00:07:29.943
has your best interest in mind.

00:07:31.230 --> 00:07:33.532
So if you are now motivated and excited

00:07:33.532 --> 00:07:37.830
to submit to your destiny
and you want further reading

